card.statement:
We often consider divided differences of products $f(x)g(y)$ of functions of $x$ and $y=x+z$. In such a case, one should keep in mind that:

\begin{align*} (f(x)g(y))_{\Delta}&=\sum\limits_{\bar{\Delta}\subseteq\Delta}\frac{(-1)^{|\bar{\Delta}|}(f(x)g(y))^{\tau_{\bar{\Delta}}}}{P_{\Delta}(x)}\\
&=\sum\limits_{\bar{\Delta}\subseteq\Delta}\frac{(-1)^{|\bar{\Delta}|}f(\tau_{\bar{\Delta}}(x))g(\tau_{\bar{\Delta}}(x)+z)}{P_{\Delta}(x)}
\end{align*}
